WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.475
At TRECVID 2026, we started with a video and a
question.

00:00:04.675 --> 00:00:09.625
One task asked us to write answers. The other asked
us to rank the supplied choices.

00:00:10.005 --> 00:00:14.186
For answer generation, our baseline sent twelve
sampled frames to Qwen.

00:00:14.386 --> 00:00:17.991
We also ran Qwen on video, with and without a
Whisper transcript.

00:00:18.191 --> 00:00:21.733
Gemini 3.7 Flash took the video with its audio.

00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:28.887
Each run returned ten ranked answers. In one run, we
put Gemini’s answer first, followed by Qwen
alternatives.

00:00:29.087 --> 00:00:34.143
For this weather question, Qwen on frames answered
“rainy.” Gemini answered “It is sunny.”

00:00:34.343 --> 00:00:40.530
“Sunny” and “It is sunny” mean the same thing here.
Their METEOR scores were 0.500 and 0.992.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:45.076
For multiple choice, matching our saved answer put
the option “Sunny” first.

00:00:45.276 --> 00:00:49.820
Direct video ranking put “Rainy” first on this
question. The scoring key was “Sunny.”

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:54.729
Across 2,428 scored questions, the picture was
different.

00:00:54.929 --> 00:01:02.971
Gemini-first scored 0.3182 on first-answer METEOR, a
wording score. That tied for second of 44 runs.

00:01:03.171 --> 00:01:11.065
Direct video ranking got 84.5% right, up from 78.7%
when we matched the saved answer.

00:01:11.265 --> 00:01:17.473
That put direct video ranking second of 42 runs,
with 140 more correct answers than matching.

00:01:17.673 --> 00:01:20.467
The paper has the results for all eight submissions.
